{
  "_about": {
    "what": "Detector latency per hardware class and accelerator, YOLOv9 t/s/m (the family the Auto tune recommender picks from) plus, in the coral columns, the one Edge TPU build a Coral runs by default (yolov9s-320-edgetpu, D908/D912). Transcribed from 2026-10-07-detector-comparison.md section (a) (Intel columns) and (f) (Apple M3 Pro, Core ML FP16 on the Neural Engine), plus the Apple M2 Mac mini bench of 2026-10-07 evening.",
    "units": "p50Ms = single-request median latency; fps = throughput ceiling of one accelerator (OpenVINO columns: 4 requests in flight; Core ML columns: 1000 / p50, the pool's Core ML executor is single-threaded).",
    "cpuColumns": "x86-cpu rows: plain ids are ONNX FP32, -int8 ids are the OpenVINO INT8 IR, both at 4 threads.",
    "m2": "apple-m-base/apple-ane: measured on a Mac mini M2 through the benchmark addon's synthetic bench (pipeline pool, predict time, 13 cameras live on the same Neural Engine, median of 3 passes) for yolov9m-320, yolov9m-640, yolov9s-640, yolov9t-640. The other cells are the M3 Pro cell x 1.2 (the measured M2 / M3 Pro ratio was 1.0-1.2) and carry measured:false.",
    "lockedBy": "packages/types/src/pipeline/auto-tune/__tests__/detector-performance.spec.ts \u2014 the TS table equals this file.",
    "amdPhoenix": "amd-phoenix/x86-cpu measured on agent-b (2026-10-10): plain ids = onnx:cpu FP32, -int8 = openvino:cpu INT8 IR; single-request warm median of 3, fps = round(1000/p50). Raw: scratchpad/detector-latency-amd-phoenix-x86-cpu-{int8,onnx}.json. amd-phoenix/amd-igpu is onnx:webgpu, re-measured on the GPU 2026-10-23 (see amdIgpuMethod).",
    "amdIgpuMethod": "scripts/bench-detector-latency-column.mjs (skill camstack-benchmark-detection): restartAddon(detection-pipeline); rearm; 1 cold + 3 warm runPipelineTest plane=frame alone; p50 = median of warm inferMs. Re-measured 2026-10-23 (all six family models, none shed) with the D845 render-node fix running: probe as uid 1001 in the agent container reported render-node=ok and providers=[WebGpuExecutionProvider], raw session.run p50 12.5 ms (t-320) and 161 ms (m-640); sysfs gpu_busy_percent rose to 20-38 % during the run. Raw: scratchpad/detector-latency-amd-phoenix-amd-igpu-20261023.json.",
    "amdIgpuStale": "The amd-phoenix/amd-igpu cells of 2026-10-10 (yolov9t-320 188 ms, slower than the ONNX CPU column at 24 ms) were the software path (D845) and were replaced on 2026-10-23; see docs/benchmarks/2026-10-10-amd-webgpu-catalog.md.",
    "n100IgpuRefresh": "intel-n-series/intel-igpu cells yolov9t-640-int8, yolov9s-640-int8, yolov9m-320-int8 and yolov9m-640-int8 were re-measured on agent-a (N100, openvino:gpu) on 2026-10-24 with scripts/bench-detector-latency-column.mjs: restartAddon(detection-pipeline), rearm, 1 cold + 3 warm runPipelineTest plane=frame object-detection alone, p50 = median of warm inferMs, fps = round(1000/p50). That fps is the single-request ceiling. The node's OpenVINO GPU pool runs one worker at concurrency 1, so the 4-in-flight fps from the 2026-10-07 transcription was not copied into these four cells. The other cells in the column are unchanged. Raw: scratchpad/lu-2026-10-24/detector-latency-intel-n-series-intel-igpu.json (gitignored). Narrative: docs/benchmarks/2026-10-24-agent-a-after-vaapi.md.",
    "coralPcie": "Coral columns (D912): ONE cell each, yolov9s-320-edgetpu, the Coral default (D908); it is YOLOv9-s at 320, so it belongs to the YOLOv9 family D745 locks the table to, and the Edge TPU 512 build and the SSD stay out. p50 32 ms / 31 fps is the SLOWEST of the three units measured on agent-b (2026-10-22: edgetpu:usb 32, edgetpu:pci 29, edgetpu:pci:1 23 ms; same harness, 1 cold + 3 warm, docs/benchmarks/2026-10-22-coral-pcie-amd-phoenix.md second section), so a PCIe unit is sized conservatively and the one cell serves every bus. amd-phoenix/coral is measured; the other hardware classes carry the same cell as measured:false (the invoke runs on the TPU, the host only adds the bus and the Python step, and no Coral was benchmarked on those hosts). A Coral is sized only when the operator ENABLED it (D39 stays: a Coral is never enabled automatically). The other measured Coral step latencies (ssd-mobilenet-v2-coco-edgetpu 14-16 ms, bird-classifier 9-10, yunet-2023mar 22-29, yolox-tiny-plate ~61) are in the same benchmark file."
  },
